st - simple terminal
--------------------
st is a simple terminal emulator for X which sucks less.

This is a personal fork of the original st project, tracked on the "v1"
branch. The changes on this branch are about personal theming only: a custom
color palette, font, and selection/cursor styling. No upstream functionality
has been removed or modified.


Changes on this branch
----------------------
- Selection colors: text selection uses dedicated, configurable background
  (defaultsb) and foreground (defaultsf) colors in config.h instead of the
  default reverse-video effect. Implemented with a new ATTR_SELECTED glyph
  attribute (st.h, x.c).
- Personal color theme: custom 16-color palette plus special colors
  (background, foreground, cursor, cursor text, selection background,
  selection foreground, badge) in config.h.
- Custom font: "FantasqueSansM Nerd Font" at size 14.
- Cursor shape: when an application resets the cursor shape (cursor 0 in
  OSC 50), st now falls back to the cursorshape value configured in config.h
  instead of the default block cursor.


Requirements
------------
In order to build st you need the Xlib header files.


Installation
------------
Edit config.mk to match your local setup (st is installed into
the /usr/local namespace by default).

Afterwards enter the following command to build and install st (if
necessary as root):

    make clean install


Running st
----------
If you did not install st with make clean install, you must compile
the st terminfo entry with the following command:

    tic -sx st.info

See the man page for additional details.

